WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.688
Detection without response shortens
the investigation, not the exposure.

2
00:00:04.688 --> 00:00:09.685
So every playbook is confidence-gated:
high confidence prepares containment,

3
00:00:09.685 --> 00:00:14.913
medium confidence enriches and tickets for
a human, and low confidence never acts.

4
00:00:14.913 --> 00:00:17.987
Responses sit on the
workbook's actuation ladder.

5
00:00:17.987 --> 00:00:19.300
L1 observes.

6
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:20.600
L2 advises.

7
00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:25.443
L3, gated actuation, is the default
for anything with a large blast radius:

8
00:00:25.443 --> 00:00:29.721
the playbook checks its preconditions
and prepares the action,

9
00:00:29.721 --> 00:00:31.900
and a named approver releases it.

10
00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:34.534
L4 runs alone, logged and reversible,

11
00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:39.187
for enumerated classes such as
closing known-benign incidents.

12
00:00:39.187 --> 00:00:43.246
Three classes stay at L3
permanently: isolating a server,

13
00:00:43.246 --> 00:00:48.426
disabling a privileged or emergency
account, and any tenant-wide change.

14
00:00:48.426 --> 00:00:51.871
Defender XDR's attack
disruption acts on its own,

15
00:00:51.871 --> 00:00:56.350
so the authorizing official
decides whether to accept it as L4.

16
00:00:56.350 --> 00:00:57.812
Latency is real.

17
00:00:57.812 --> 00:01:02.980
Session revocation can take up to 15
minutes in services that support continuous

18
00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:07.843
access evaluation, and a hybrid user must
be disabled in Active Directory too,

19
00:01:07.843 --> 00:01:10.340
or the next synchronization undoes it.
